{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlockIsospinLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlockIsospinLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_gradient_at_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_gradient_at_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L79-L85","doc":"**Theorem 3.** The first-order deformation gradient of the mass anomaly at `q=1`\nextracts the exact Plancherel weight 1/24. This proves that the\nleading-order scale of the nucleon split is purely topological. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_gradient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_gradient","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The deformation gradient `Δτ_M(q) / (q - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_vanishes_at_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_vanishes_at_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**Theorem 2.** The classical vanishing of the isospin mass anomaly.\nAt `q=1`, the proton and neutron are mathematically identical (isospin symmetry).\nThe empirical mass split `Δm_{np}` is exclusively a q-deformation effect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.delta_tau_M_poly","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The categorical mass anomaly between the proton and neutron.\nProportional to the Hecke deformation `(q - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.trace_baryon_braid_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.trace_baryon_braid_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L58-L61","doc":"The trace evaluates to 1 at the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.trace_baryon_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.trace_baryon_braid","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L52-L56","doc":"The trace of the 6-crossing Borromean baryon braid\n`β = σ₀σ₁σ₂σ₀σ₁σ₂` on the sign block.\nIn the sign representation, `σ_i ↦ -q⁻¹`, so `β ↦ (-q⁻¹)^6 = q⁻⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.wenzl_sign_h4_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.wenzl_sign_h4_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L46-L50","doc":"**Theorem 1.** The classical Plancherel weight of the sign block in S_4 is 1/24.\nProves that the q-deformed Wenzl weight smoothly recovers the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.wenzl_sign_h4_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.wenzl_sign_h4_poly","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L41-L44","doc":"The Wenzl weight for the (1,1,1,1) sign block of H_4(q).\n`d_q(1^4) = 1`, so the weight is `1 / [4]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.q_int_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.H4SignBlock.q_int_poly","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/H4SignBlockIsospinLimit.lean#L32-L39","doc":"The rational polynomial surrogate for the unnormalized q-integer [n]_q.\nThis avoids the 0/0 singularity at q=1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}